8-Wulf2"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wulf</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Markenstein</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>van der Linden</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Voss</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Klaassen</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>First outbreak of MRSA ST398 in a Dutch hospital.</article-title><comment>18th European Congress of Clinical Microbiology and Infectious Diseases, April 19&#x02013;22, Barcelona, Spain</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004258-1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>USDA National Agriculture Statistics Service</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004258-Honeyman1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Honeyman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Duffy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Iowa's Changing Swine Industry.</article-title><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.econ.iastate.edu/research/webpapers/paper_12581.pdf">http://www.econ.iastate.edu/research/webpapers/paper_12581.pdf</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004258-Ince1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ince</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Winokur</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Beekmann</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Herwaldt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfaller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Prevalence of Panton Valentine Leukocidin genes among methicillin-resistant <italic>Staphylococcus aureus</italic> in Iowa.</article-title><comment>Society for Healthcare Epidemiology of America 15th Annual Scientific Meeting, April 9&#x02013;12, Los Angeles, CA</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004258-VandeGriend1"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van de Griend</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Herwaldt</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Alvis</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Demartino</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Heilmann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Community-associated methicillin-resistant <italic>Staphylococcus aureus</italic> (CA-MRSA): an emerging cause of bloodstream infection (BSI) in Iowa.</article-title><comment>47th Interscience Conference on Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy, September 17&#x02013;20, Chicago, IL</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004258-vanLoo2"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Loo</surname><given-names>IH</given-names></name><name><surname>Diederen</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Savelkoul</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Woudenberg</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Roosendaal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Methicillin-resistant <italic>Staphylococcus aureus</italic> in meat products, the Netherlands.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>1753</fpage><lpage>1755</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18217563</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This study was funded with departmental startup funds (TCS). The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>